# Terraform
#
# State files record every attribute of every resource, including values AWS
# generates and any secret passed into a resource, in plain text. They are also
# environment-specific. Neither belongs in version control.
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl.bak
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json

# Saved plans. `terraform plan -out=FILE` writes every resource attribute the
# plan touches, in the clear, including values marked sensitive in console
# output. Nothing ignored these before, so a saved plan was the one Terraform
# artifact that could be committed by accident.
*.tfplan
tfplan
plan.out

crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# Credentials and key material
#
# None of these exist in this repository and none ever has. They are listed so
# that if one ever appears — copied in to debug something, generated by a tool,
# dropped in by mistake — it cannot be staged without someone overriding the
# ignore on purpose. The cost of being wrong here is a public key leak, so the
# patterns are broad rather than minimal.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
id_dsa*
.aws/credentials
.aws/config
